- Draft derived from the sprint authoring worktree at `/tmp/msc-math-unlimited-20260907.IvqpRR/authoring`; no external-source verification or computational rerun performed.
- `thesis/07-hko-local-maximum.tex`: theorem scope, Hausdorff topology, ratio value, equality orbit, HKO representative and convention reconciliation. The compact definition here uses that reconciled representative; the full source explains its relation to the opposite symplectic-form convention in the HKO paper.
- `thesis/07-hko-local-maximum-chart-reduction.tex`: local polar-vertex chart, 40 coordinates, 15-dimensional symmetry orbit and local transverse slice.
- `thesis/07-hko-local-maximum-exact-certificate.tex`: normalized feasible upper functions; 26 rows, quotient rank 25, positive relation; necessity of singular seven-facet data; exact verifier and Rust witness roles.
- The one-dimensional bound example is elementary explanatory material introduced for this candidate, not a figure or model reported by the HKO source. A possible schematic would draw only the two lines and their lower envelope; a hypothetical `f` curve is unnecessary and could imply unsupported equality.
- Intended comparison: importance/theorem first, then a minimal mechanism, with coordinate bookkeeping deferred until its role is apparent. This is an exploratory alternative, not a controlled causal experiment isolating one variable.
